00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.630 align:start position:0%
the world is making adjustments  following a new and even more infectious  strain of the coronavirus spreading in  the united kingdom and beyond  it comes with nearly 80 million known  infections around the world  resulting in at least 1.7 million deaths  holly williams has more on the global  impact of the pandemic this morning  there were no crowds in the vatican  saint peter's square yesterday  when normally they gather in their tens  of thousands to hear the pope's  christmas blessing  no worshipers in notre dame cathedral in  paris  though they did broadcast this concert  recorded in the medieval structure  damaged by a fire last year  and here in london many people felt that  christmas had effectively been  cancelled as we saw earlier this week in  the city's commercial heart  the government says the country has  entered its worst recession  in 300 years this is oxford street  normally  the busiest shopping street in all of  europe as you can see  it is eerily quiet after a new mutated  version of the virus  was discovered here in the uk and london  went into strict lockdown  the authorities here said the new strain  was more infectious  a heartbreaking christmas for millions  of people mixing between  households including on christmas day  was banned  for christians queen elizabeth gave her  traditional christmas day message from  windsor castle  where she's social distancing in  splendor in the united kingdom  and around the world people have risen  magnificently to the challenges of the  year  but for thousands of truck drivers left  stranded on the roadside  when france closed its border to the uk  there wasn't much to celebrate  just frustration and anger  for christians this festival is a time  of hope  symbolized by the birth of the baby  jesus  and amongst the despair and the  loneliness there is  hope this christmas for billions of  people  of all faiths it comes in the form of a  vaccine  in the pope's christmas day address  yesterday to a small socially distanced  group  he called for international cooperation  by governments and businesses  to make sure that everyone gets access  to vaccines for covert 19  especially the most vulnerable and the  needy the pope said quote  we cannot erect walls all of us are in  the same boat  jerica holly williams thank you
 

